second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the genre of the film \\\"Bright Lights\\\"?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 132, \"text\": \"Bright Lights (1928 film) Bright Lights is a 1928 silent cartoon short by Walt Disney Productions featuring Oswald the Lucky Rabbit.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00\", \"start\": 133, \"end\": 226, \"text\": \"It is among the few short films of the series Disney worked on before leaving that same year.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00\", \"start\": 227, \"end\": 324, \"text\": \"Previously in 1927, Oswald had an oval face, a chubbier waist, and pants with a single suspender.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00\", \"start\": 325, \"end\": 408, \"text\": \"By 1928, he's given a makeover, having a rounder head, a slimmer waist, and shorts.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00\", \"start\": 409, \"end\": 513, \"text\": \"Despite this change, the rabbit's 1927 appearance would still appear on the title cards until \\\"High Up\\\".\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00\", \"start\": 514, \"end\": 561, \"text\": \"His shorts would be his only outfit until 1930.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00\", \"start\": 562, \"end\": 577, \"text\": \"A show composed\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 126, \"text\": \"Bright Lights (1928 film) Bright Lights is a 1928 romantic drama by Walt Disney Productions featuring Oswald the Lucky Rabbit.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d01\", \"start\": 127, \"end\": 220, \"text\": \"It is among the few short films of the series Disney worked on before leaving that same year.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d01\", \"start\": 221, \"end\": 318, \"text\": \"Previously in 1927, Oswald had an oval face, a chubbier waist, and pants with a single suspender.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d01\", \"start\": 319, \"end\": 402, \"text\": \"By 1928, he's given a makeover, having a rounder head, a slimmer waist, and shorts.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d01\", \"start\": 403, \"end\": 507, \"text\": \"Despite this change, the rabbit's 1927 appearance would still appear on the title cards until \\\"High Up\\\".\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d01\", \"start\": 508, \"end\": 555, \"text\": \"His shorts would be his only outfit until 1930.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d01\", \"start\": 556, \"end\": 574, \"text\": \"A show composed...\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 211, \"text\": \"Bright Lights (1930 film) Bright Lights is a 1930 American pre-Code musical comedy film photographed entirely in Technicolor and produced and released by First National Pictures, a subsidiary of Warner Brothers.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d02\", \"start\": 212, \"end\": 333, \"text\": \"Although filmed in December 1929, the film sat on the shelf until the autumn of 1930 when it was given a limited release.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d02\", \"start\": 334, \"end\": 446, \"text\": \"However, Warners quickly withdrew the film when the studio realized that the public had grown weary of musicals.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d02\", \"start\": 447, \"end\": 620, \"text\": \"Warners believed that this attitude would only last for a few months, but, when the public proved obstinate, they reluctantly re-released the film early in 1931 after making\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 16, \"text\": \"on May 14, 2016.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d03\", \"start\": 17, \"end\": 159, \"text\": \"It was also screened at the Telluride Film Festival on September 3, 2016 and at the Hot Springs Documentary Film Festival on October 14, 2016.\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d03\", \"start\": 160, \"end\": 269, \"text\": \"It went on to screen at the New York Film Festival on October 10, 2016 and the AFI Fest on November 13, 2016.\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d03\", \"start\": 270, \"end\": 443, \"text\": \"The documentary was to premiere on HBO in March 2017, but after the actresses' deaths in late December 2016, the network announced that they were reconsidering the air date.\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d03\", \"start\": 444, \"end\": 525, \"text\": \"The decision was subsequently made to air the premiere on HBO on January 7, 2017.\"}, \"D4S6\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d03\", \"start\": 526, \"end\": 557, \"text\": \"\\\"Bright Lights: Starring Carrie\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0485-53896a80bcfa:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Bright Lights\", \"scope\": \"film\", \"claim\": \"The genre of the film \\\"Bright Lights\\\" is cartoon.\", \"answer\": \"cartoo